 class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-circle-question-mark w-5 h-5 text-[#00AEEF]" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><path d="M9.09 9a3 3 0 0 1 5.83 1c0 2-3 3-3 3"></path><path d="M12 17h.01"></path></svg><h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-black">Frequently Asked Questions</h3></div><p class="text-sm md:text-base text-gray-600">Common questions about this tool and how to use it effectively</p></div><div class="bg-white rounded-lg border border-gray-200 p-4 md:p-6"><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">1</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What is an SSL certificate and why is it important?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>An SSL/TLS certificate encrypts data transmitted between your website and visitors, protecting sensitive information like passwords and payment details. It's essential for security, user trust, and SEO - Google marks HTTP sites as 'Not Secure' and uses HTTPS as a ranking factor. All modern websites must have a valid SSL certificate.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">2</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">How often should I check my SSL certificate?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Check your SSL certificate monthly, especially 60-90 days before expiration. Many certificates are valid for 90 days (Let's Encrypt) or 1 year. Set up automated monitoring or renewal to prevent expiration, which causes browser warnings and breaks user trust. Most hosting providers offer auto-renewal for SSL certificates.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">3</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What does 'certificate chain invalid' mean?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Certificate chain validation ensures your SSL certificate is properly linked to a trusted Certificate Authority (CA). An invalid chain means intermediate certificates are missing or misconfigured. This causes browser security warnings even if your certificate is valid. Contact your SSL provider or hosting company to fix certificate chain issues.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">4</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">Is a self-signed SSL certificate safe to use?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Self-signed certificates provide encryption but aren't trusted by browsers - visitors see scary security warnings. They're fine for internal testing or development environments, but NEVER use them on public websites. Use free certificates from Let's Encrypt or paid certificates from trusted CAs (DigiCert, Sectigo, GlobalSign) for production sites.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">5</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">What SSL/TLS protocol version should I use?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Use TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.3 (latest and most secure). Older protocols (SSL 2.0, SSL 3.0, TLS 1.0, TLS 1.1) have known vulnerabilities and are deprecated. Modern browsers and servers support TLS 1.2+ by default. Disable older protocols in your server configuration to maintain strong security.</p></div></div><div class="border-b border-gray-200 last:border-0"><button class="w-full py-6 flex items-start gap-4 text-left hover:bg-gray-50 -mx-4 px-4 rounded-lg transition-colors duration-200"><div class="flex-shrink-0 w-8 h-8 bg-[#00AEEF]/10 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center"><span class="text-sm font-bold text-[#00AEEF]">6</span></div><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><h3 class="text-base md:text-lg font-semibold text-black">My SSL certificate is expiring soon - what should I do?</h3></div><div class="flex-shrink-0"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-down w-5 h-5 text-gray-400" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"></path></svg></div></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-4 pb-6 text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed" style="padding-left:3.5rem"><p>Renew your certificate immediately if it expires in less than 30 days. Most SSL providers send renewal reminders 60-90 days before expiration. If using Let's Encrypt, enable auto-renewal via Certbot. If using a paid certificate, renew through your provider. After renewal, update your server configuration and verify the new certificate is active.</p></div></div></div><div class="mt-6 text-center"><p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2">Still have questions?</p><a href="/contact" class="text-[#00AEEF] font-semibold hover:underline inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm md:text-base">Contact our team for help<svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2.5" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3"></path></svg></a></div></div><section class="py-12 bg-[#F5F5F5]"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4"><div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-2xl px-6 py-8 md:py-10" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1a1a 0%, #0a0a0a 100%)"><div class="absolute inset-0 z-0" style="background-image:linear-gradient(rgba(255,255,255,0.1) 1px, transparent 1px),
